  "callouts": [
    {
      "id": "step-1",
      "kind": "step",
      "text": "1 · Click the violet Async region. Press Communication — cards go Simple, cables go Summary, and the DRAW group appears.",
      "x": 100,
      "y": 300,
      "w": 420,
      "h": 160,
      "target": {
        "shapeId": "region",
        "anchor": "left",
        "dy": -280
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-2",
      "kind": "step",
      "text": "2 · Press Service, drag Mission's card onto Robot's. No ports, no port dots. Repeat with Action. Then Stream, Camera → Mission.",
      "x": 100,
      "y": 520,
      "w": 420,
      "h": 170,
      "target": {
        "shapeId": "mission",
        "anchor": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-3",
      "kind": "step",
      "text": "3 · CABLES › Split. One arrow becomes its protocol legs, each tagged with its phase. Summary puts them back — it always rides the request, or the goal.",
      "x": 100,
      "y": 750,
      "w": 420,
      "h": 190,
      "target": {
        "shapeId": "region",
        "anchor": "left",
        "dy": 140
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-4",
      "kind": "step",
      "text": "4 · Press Dataflow. Cards go Port, cables go Data, and every socket is back on a left or right lane — Dataflow has no top or bottom edge.",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 320,
      "w": 420,
      "h": 180,
      "target": {
        "shapeId": "robot",
        "anchor": "right",
        "dy": -60
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-5",
      "kind": "step",
      "text": "5 · Still in Dataflow, CABLES › Summary. The relationship arrows come back over the real routes and no port moves.",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 560,
      "w": 420,
      "h": 160,
      "target": {
        "shapeId": "robot",
        "anchor": "right",
        "dy": 60
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-6",
      "kind": "step",
      "text": "6 · Back in Communication with CARD › P, press and HOLD a port dot on Camera, then drag it to any of the four edges. Hold still first — moving straight away draws a cable instead.",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 860,
      "w": 420,
      "h": 210,
      "target": {
        "shapeId": "camera",
        "anchor": "right"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "pass",
      "kind": "pass",
      "text": "PASS WHEN the two lenses disagree about where a port is and neither disturbs the other. CARD S/P/E works in both. CABLES Data/Split/Summary changes only paint, never a port position. A socket dragged in Communication can sit on any of the four edges, its cable follows it, and Dataflow still shows it on a lane.",
      "x": 620,
      "y": 1290,
      "w": 1080,
      "h": 260
    }
